      "title": "Research on pressure reduction methods for micro-flow control systems in gravitational wave detection",
      "abstract": "This paper investigates the pressure reduction performance of three types of pressure-reducing valves—mechanical, piezo-electric proportional, and Bang-bang valves—for micro-flow control systems used in space gravitational wave detection missions. An experimental micro-flow control platform was established to systematically analyze the pressure characteristics, flow stability, and flow-induced noise performance of each valve under different flow conditions. The results demonstrate that the mechanical pressure-reducing valve exhibits minimal pressure fluctuation and stable flow output within the range of 0.03–0.4 sccm, with flow-induced noise below 0.1 μg/s/√Hz in the frequency band of 1mHz–1Hz, meeting the stringent noise requirements for gravitational wave detection. In contrast, both the piezo-electric proportional and Bang-bang valves induce significant flow fluctuations due to inherent pressure pulsations caused by their control mechanisms. Therefore, mechanical pressure-reducing valves are more suitable for micro-flow control systems in high-precision gravitational wave detection missions.",
