  "stdout": "# Novel Autonomous Dispersal Systems for High-Density Granular Payloads\n\n## Technical Proposal: Shear-Amplified Resonant Acoustic Dispersal (SARD) System\n\n---\n\n## Background & Motivation\n\n### The Challenge of Granular Dispersal from Aerial Platforms\n\nModern environmental remediation, precision agriculture, ecological restoration, and advanced fire suppression increasingly require the aerial delivery of specialized granular agents—mineral-based sorbents, microbial seeds, or novel powder-based retardants. These applications demand precise, uniform distribution over defined areas with minimal environmental contamination.\n\n### Limitations of Current Systems\n\nExisting aerial dispersal systems suffer from fundamental limitations when handling high-density, fine-grained powders:\n\n- **Rotary spreaders** (centrifugal disc designs): Provide poor spatial uniformity, especially at varying flight velocities. Performance degrades significantly with cohesive, fine powders that exhibit bridging and rat-holing in hoppers.\n\n- **Vibratory feeders**: Traditional mechanical vibration (eccentric motors) introduces excessive weight, creates parasitic structural loads on the drone airframe, and produces inconsistent flow rates with cohesive materials due to non-uniform acceleration fields.\n\n---\n| \\( \\vec{k} \\) | Acoustic wavevector | rad/m |\n| \\( \\alpha \\) | Attenuation coefficient | 1/m |\n| \\( V_f \\) | Drone forward velocity | m/s |\n| \\( s \\) | Flight pass spacing | m |\n| \\( t_{disp} \\) | Dispersion time constant | s |\n| \\( \\delta_w \\) | Lateral spreading width | m |\n\n---\n\n*This proposal describes the Shear-Amplified Resonant Acoustic Dispersal (SARD) system, a fundamentally novel approach to aerial granular dispersal that has not been previously proposed in the literature. The combination of programmable standing wave fluidization, acoustic-phase-gated release valves, and drone-motion entrainment represents a new class of dispersal mechanism with application potential across environmental remediation, precision agriculture, fire suppression, and ecological restoration.*\n",
